"Meta AI gains momentum with Zuckerberg's agent for the masses (https://www.axios.com/2026/09/18/meta-muse-personal-agent-make-money)\nciteturn843news12 [wordlim: 100] Published: today; Date: Fri Sep 18 15:35:09 2026 UTC ... Meta's Muse is rocketing up the app charts with a distinctly practical vision for AI - an agent that can shop, haggle, cancel subscriptions and clear away the digital drudgery of everyday life.\nMeta AI gains momentum with Zuckerberg's agent for the masses\nDate: Fri Sep 18 15:35:09 2026 UTC\n\nMeta AI gains momentum with Zuckerberg's agent for the masses\n\nMeta's Muse is rocketing up the app charts with a distinctly practical vision for AI - an agent that can shop, haggle, cancel subscriptions and clear away the digital drudgery of everyday life.\nWhy it matters: Mark Zuckerberg is staking Meta's AI comeback on one of the enduring strengths of his internet empire: making new technology feel native to billions of ordinary people.\nState of play: Ten days after launch, Muse is the No. 1 free iPhone app in America, leading ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Instagram and everything else on the App Store.\nThe big picture: Muse poses an early test of whether Meta's structural advantages - product design, distribution and an intimate grasp of consumer behavior - can shape the AI race more than raw intelligence alone.\nZoom in: Meta chief AI officer Alexandr Wang has spent the past week curating a highlight reel of Muse wins, with one pitch surfacing again and again: this thing can save you money.\nThe intrigue: Meta is testing a voice feature that allows Muse to make phone calls on a user's behalf - one of the clearest glimpses yet of AI agents becoming real-world stand-ins for their users.\nReality check: The more useful Muse becomes, the more of your life it needs to see: email, calendars, financial accounts, purchases, contacts and eventually even the phone calls it makes in your name.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nClaude Cowork and chat are now one Claude | Claude by Anthropic (https://claude.com/blog/cowork-is-now-claude)\nciteturn843search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: today; # Claude Cowork and chat are now one Claude ... September 16, 2026\n\n# Claude Cowork and chat are now one Claude\n\nYou don’t have to choose where a task goes. Claude does more of the work.\n\n  * Category\n\nProduct announcements\n\n  * Product\n\nClaude apps\n\nClaude Cowork\n\n  * Date\n\nSeptember 16, 2026\n\n  * Reading time\n\n5\n\nmin\n\n  * Share\n\nCopy link\n\nhttps://claude.com/blog/cowork-is-now-claude\n\nStarting today, Claude Cowork and chat are merging into one Claude. Bring a quick question, or hand over a report due at noon, and Claude takes it from there, even after you’ve closed your laptop. It’s rolling out on Pro and Max plans over the next few weeks, with more plans to follow.\n\nWhat Claude makes doesn’t need its own place either. Claude Docs and Claude Slides are new today, and Claude Design now works inside your conversations too. Ask for a document, and you and Claude write it together. Ask for a presentation, and Claude drafts the slides. You can edit directly, present straight from Claude, or download as PowerPoint or PDF. All three are in beta on paid plans, and Enterprise admins choose when to turn them on. If you use Claude Design on its own, it keeps working as before. \n\nClaude Cowork and chat are now one Claude\n\nWe built Cowork as a separate place for bigger work, and Design for visual work. People used both, and told us the frustrating part was deciding where a task belonged. What they’d started in one also didn’t carry into the other. So we stopped making you choose. Claude can now figure out what a task needs, so what Cowork and Design can do is available from any conversation, with the context, skills, and connectors you already have. \n\n> “I could have Claude pull up [my legal research database], and it would pull all the cases, read them, figure out which other cases I might need, download them, and store them in a folder for my personal review.” - Andrew Keller, Senior Economist\n\n## What it looks like\n\nA weekly report is due at noon. Before you head out, you ask Claude what moved in the pipeline last week, then add: “Write it the way we always do, flag anything that slipped, and put the highlights in five slides for the leadership meeting.” --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntroducing Muse: The World’s First Personal AI Agent Built for Everyone (https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/)\nciteturn843search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: today; September 8, 2026September 8, 2026 ... https://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Introducing-Muse_Sizzle-Video.mp4 ... Because personal agents need a new kind of secure computer, Muse runs on Muse Secure VM, a dedicated, virtual machine (VM) that houses both the agent and a person’s data.\n\nBack to Newsroom\n\nMeta\n\n# Introducing Muse: The World’s First Personal AI Agent Built for Everyone\n\nSeptember 8, 2026September 8, 2026\n\nListen to Article 10 Pause 10\n\n[Select]\n\nhttps://about.fb.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Introducing-Muse_Sizzle-Video.mp4\n\n## Takeaways\n\n  * Muse is a personal AI agent. It doesn’t just answer questions, it actually does the work. It helps people stay on top of things, takes tasks and projects off their plate, and turns long-term goals into action plans.\n  * Meta built Muse from the ground up to be a safe, secure, private, and widely available personal AI agent.\n  * Muse runs on Muse Secure VM, a dedicated secure computer with its own browser, and can work on a person’s behalf across the apps they use daily, learning from conversations, reflecting on what matters to them, and getting sharper along the way.\n  * Each person stays in control of their Muse and decides how much access it gets. \n  * For a deeper look at how Muse was designed and how safety, security, and privacy were built into it, read How We Built Safety Into Muse and How We Designed Muse.\n\nToday, Meta is introducing Muse, a secure, private personal AI agent that proactively helps with people’s goals and suggests ideas. Because personal agents need a new kind of secure computer, Muse runs on Muse Secure VM, a dedicated, virtual machine (VM) that houses both the agent and a person’s data. Muse is designed around the way people already communicate, so talking to it works just like messaging another person, in the Muse app or directly in WhatsApp.\n\nIt’s simple to use. People just tell Muse what needs to get done, and it takes action, powered by Muse Spark, Meta’s most capable model to date, built for real-world agentic work like this. \n\n## How It Works\n\nUnlike other agents, Muse was built to work for billions of people worldwide, so there’s no learning curve. Anyone can use it out of the box, no technical experience required. It can handle tasks, like sending an email or booking travel, and it can take on big audacious goals. Once a person shares a goal with Muse, it helps them develop a personalized plan and coordinate their time and resources, then advances the work on its own. It can open a browser, fill out forms, and negotiate on their behalf.\n\nFor tasks that take more time, Muse keeps working after people close the app, and comes back when something changes or when it needs approval, like before it sends an email or makes a purchase. It gets better results with less effort: selling a car for more, lowering a bill, adjusting a training plan as the rest of someone’s life shifts.\n\nWhen it comes time to pay, Muse can checkout with Link built by Stripe, and it is the first AI agent covered by Link’s purchase protections: free coverage for damaged or lost items, price drops, no-fee returns, and a return guarantee on eligible purchases. Link’s wallet for agents generates a one-time-use card so your real card details stay hidden, allowing you to purchase safely across the internet. Shop Pay is coming soon as another way to pay, along with 1Password support so Muse can use logins a person already has. \n\nMuse also remembers what matters to a person, so it can make suggestions unprompted and act on details that person only mentioned once. It can turn a recipe reel the person saved on Instagram into a grocery list, suggest a menu for their dinner party, and remember their friends’ dietary restrictions before it sends the invites.\n\n## Built to be Private, Safe, and Secure\n\nPersonal agents need a new kind of secure computer, so Meta built one for everyone. Muse Secure VM has first-of-its-kind privacy, safety, and security protections engineered into it that no other agent provides:\n\n  * Muse runs on its own dedicated computer in the cloud, contained so no one else’s agent can reach it. That is where Muse lives and where the data and credentials for any service a person connects are securely stored.\n  * A separate Sentinel agent runs on that same machine, kept apart from Muse at the system level. Nothing Muse does reaches the internet unless the Sentinel approves it, and it asks the person for permission when needed.\n  * Muse has no visibility into people’s passwords or payment methods. Any credentials a person shares go into secure storage, so Muse can use them without seeing them, including passwords a person types into the browser themselves. \n  * Muse checks with the person before sensitive actions like sending an email or making a purchase. Muse shows people a complete audit trail of everything it has done and plans to do. \n  * People choose which apps Muse connects to and exactly how much access it gets. For things like email, people choose what Muse can do, whether it reads their mail or can also send on their behalf. \n  * People can change access or disconnect a service whenever they want. People can also opt out of their interactions being used to train Meta’s AI models.\n  * Muse doesn’t share a person’s conversations or the data in their VM with Meta’s ad systems. \n  * Muse remembers what matters to a person, and they can always tell it to “forget” specific things it’s learned.\n\nLater this year, Meta will introduce Muse Confidential VM, where the whole VM, including a person’s data and conversations with Muse, is encrypted with a key only they hold, so not even Meta can access it.\n\n## Looking Ahead\n\nMeta thinks personal superintelligence will be one of the most transformative technologies of a lifetime. Muse is a first step: an agent that takes on more of the work so people can focus on what matters to them.\n\nMuse is rolling out in the US on iOS, Android, and muse.ai, and coming soon to AI glasses. It’s free for most of what people need, with subscription plans for people who want to do more.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPresentamos Muse: el primer agente de IA personal del mundo creado para todos | Acerca de Meta (https://about.fb.com/ltam/news/2026/09/presentamos-muse-el-primer-agente-de-ia-personal-del-mundo-creado-para-todos/)\nciteturn843search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: today; # Presentamos Muse: el primer agente de IA personal del mundo creado para todosseptiembre 8, 2026septiembre 8, 2026\n\nBack to Newsroom\n\nMeta\n\n# Presentamos Muse: el primer agente de IA personal del mundo creado para todos\n\nseptiembre 8, 2026septiembre 8, 2026\n\n## Puntos clave:\n\n  * Muse es un agente de IA personal. No solo responde preguntas: hace el trabajo. Ayuda a las personas a mantener todo bajo control, se hace cargo de tareas y proyectos, y convierte metas de largo plazo en planes de acción.\n  * Meta construyó Muse desde cero para que sea un agente de IA personal seguro, protegido, privado y ampliamente disponible.\n  * Muse funciona sobre Muse Secure VM, una computadora segura dedicada con su propio navegador, y puede trabajar en nombre de cada persona en las apps que usa a diario, aprendiendo de las conversaciones, reflexionando sobre lo que le importa y volviéndose más preciso en el camino.\n  * Cada persona mantiene el control de su Muse y decide cuánto acceso le da.\n  * Para conocer en profundidad cómo se diseñó Muse y cómo se integraron la seguridad, la protección y la privacidad, lee Cómo integramos la seguridad en Muse y Cómo diseñamos Muse.\n\nHoy, Meta presentó Muse, un agente de IA personal seguro y privado que ayuda de forma proactiva con las metas de las personas y sugiere ideas. Debido a que los agentes personales necesitan un nuevo tipo de computadora segura, Muse funciona sobre Muse Secure VM, una máquina virtual (VM) dedicada que aloja tanto al agente como los datos de la persona. Muse está diseñado en torno a la forma en que las personas ya se comunican, así que hablar con él es igual que enviar un mensaje a otra persona, ya sea en la app de Muse o directamente en WhatsApp.\n\nEs simple de usar. Las personas solo le dicen a Muse qué necesitan que se haga, y él actúa, impulsado por Muse Spark, el modelo más capaz de Meta hasta la fecha, creado para el trabajo agéntico del mundo real.\n\nCómo funciona\n\nA diferencia de otros agentes, Muse fue creado para funcionar para miles de millones de personas en todo el mundo, así que no hay curva de aprendizaje. Cualquiera puede usarlo de entrada, sin necesidad de experiencia técnica. Puede encargarse de tareas como enviar un correo electrónico o reservar un viaje, y también asumir metas grandes y ambiciosas. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConheça o Muse: o primeiro agente de IA pessoal do mundo, feito para todos | Sobre a Meta (https://about.fb.com/br/news/2026/09/conheca-o-muse-o-primeiro-agente-de-ia-pessoal-do-mundo-feito-para-todos/)\nciteturn843search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: today; https://about.fb.com/br/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2026/09/Muse-Sizzle-16x9-1.mp4\n\nVoltar para Newsroom\n\nMeta\n\n# Conheça o Muse: o primeiro agente de IA pessoal do mundo, feito para todos\n\n08/09/202608/09/2026\n\n## Destaques\n\n  * O Muse é um agente de IA pessoal. Ele não apenas responde perguntas, ele realmente executa o trabalho. Ele ajuda as pessoas a manterem tudo sob controle, assume tarefas e projetos que estavam com elas e transforma metas de longo prazo em planos de ação.\n  * A Meta desenvolveu o Muse do zero para ser um agente de IA pessoal seguro, protegido, privado e amplamente disponível.\n  * O Muse funciona no Muse Secure VM, um computador seguro e dedicado com seu próprio navegador, e pode trabalhar em nome de uma pessoa nos aplicativos que ela usa no dia a dia, aprendendo com as conversas, refletindo sobre o que é importante para ela e ficando cada vez mais afiado ao longo do caminho.\n  * Cada pessoa mantém o controle do seu Muse e decide quanto acesso ele terá.\n  * Para conhecer em mais detalhes como o Muse foi projetado e como a segurança, a proteção e a privacidade foram incorporadas a ele, leia Como Incorporamos Segurança ao Muse e Como Projetamos o Muse.\n\nhttps://about.fb.com/br/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2026/09/Muse-Sizzle-16x9-1.mp4\n\nHoje, a Meta está apresentando o Muse, um agente de IA pessoal seguro e privado que ajuda de forma proativa os objetivos das pessoas e sugere ideias. Como os agentes pessoais precisam de um novo tipo de computador seguro, o Muse funciona no Muse Secure VM, uma máquina virtual (VM) dedicada que hospeda tanto o agente quanto os dados da pessoa. O Muse foi projetado em torno da forma como as pessoas já se comunicam, então conversar com ele é como enviar mensagens para outra pessoa, no app do Muse ou diretamente no WhatsApp.\n\nÉ simples de usar. As pessoas apenas dizem ao Muse o que precisa ser feito, e ele age, com a tecnologia do Muse Spark, o modelo mais capaz da Meta até hoje, criado para trabalho agêntico no mundo real como esse.\n\nComo funciona\n\nDiferentemente de outros agentes, o Muse foi criado para funcionar para bilhões de pessoas no mundo inteiro, então não há curva de aprendizado. Para coisas como e-mail, as pessoas escolhem o que o Muse pode fazer: se ele apenas lê as mensagens ou se também pode enviar em nome delas.\n  * As pessoas podem alterar o acesso ou desconectar um serviço quando quiserem. Também podem optar por não ter suas interações usadas para treinar os modelos de IA da Meta.\n  * O Muse não compartilha as conversas da pessoa nem os dados na VM dela com os sistemas de anúncios da Meta.\n  * O Muse lembra o que é importante para cada pessoa, e ela pode, a qualquer momento, pedir que ele “esqueça” coisas específicas que aprendeu.\n\nhttps://about.fb.com/br/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2026/09/Muse_Shopping.mp4\n\nAinda este ano, a Meta vai lançar o Muse Confidential VM, no qual toda a VM — incluindo os dados da pessoa e suas conversas com o Muse — é criptografada com uma chave que somente ela possui, de modo que nem a Meta consegue acessá-la.\n\nO que vem a seguir\n\nA Meta acredita que a superinteligência pessoal será uma das tecnologias mais transformadoras de uma geração. O Muse é um primeiro passo: um agente que assume mais do trabalho para que as pessoas possam se concentrar no que é importante para elas.\n\nO Muse está sendo lançado nos Estados Unidos no iOS, no Android e em muse.ai, e chega em breve aos óculos com IA. É gratuito para a maior parte do que as pessoas precisam, com planos de assinatura para quem quiser fazer mais.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMuse登場：すべての方のために構築された世界初のパーソナルAIエージェント | Metaについて (https://about.fb.com/ja/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/)\nciteturn843search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: today; https://about.fb.com/ja/wp-content/uploads/sites/15/2026/09/Muse_Shopping.mp4\n\nBack to Newsroom\n\nMeta\n\n# Muse登場：すべての方のために構築された世界初のパーソナルAIエージェント\n\n2026年09月09日2026年09月09日\n\nMetaは9月8日（米国時間）、安全性かつプライバシーに配慮したパーソナル AI エージェント「Muse」を発表しました。Muse は、利用者の目標達成を能動的にサポートし、アイデアを提案します。パーソナルエージェントには新しいタイプのセキュアなコンピューターが必要となり、Museは「Muse Secure VM」上で動作します。（英文のみ）。これは、エージェントと利用者のデータの両方を格納する専用の仮想マシン（VM）です。Muse は、利用者が普段行っているコミュニケーションのあり方に沿って設計されており、Museアプリまたは WhatsAppから、まるで他の人にメッセージを送るのと同じように対話できます。\n\n使い方はとてもシンプルです。--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUse Claude Cowork on Team and Enterprise plans | Claude Help Center (https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13455879-use-claude-cowork-on-team-and-enterprise-plans)\nciteturn843search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Note: Claude Cowork and chat are now one Claude, rolling out gradually to Pro and Max plans. ... On Enterprise plans, it's off by default at launch and turns on by default starting September 10, 2026, unless you've turned it off.\n\n# Use Claude Cowork on Team and Enterprise plans\n\nUpdated today\n\nCopy for LLM\n\nNote: Claude Cowork and chat are now one Claude, rolling out gradually to Pro and Max plans. Ask for what you need, and Claude decides whether that's a quick answer or a task. Team and Enterprise organizations keep chat and Claude Cowork as they are today, so everything in this article still applies. Learn more in our blog post.\n\nThis article explains important limitations and considerations for Team and Enterprise organizations using Claude Cowork.\n\n## Availability\n\nClaude Cowork is available on paid plans (Pro, Max, Team, Enterprise). Availability varies by surface:\n\n  * Claude Desktop for macOS — Available on all paid plans. Click here to download.\n\n  * Claude Desktop for Windows — Available on all paid plans. Cowork requires the latest version of Claude for Windows. Download or update at claude.com/download.\n\n  * Web (beta), at claude.ai — Available on Pro, Max, and Team plans. \n  * Enterprise plans: off by default. An owner turns on \"Run Cowork in the cloud,\" then grants the Cowork in the cloud capability to a group with custom roles. See Manage custom roles on Enterprise plans.\n\n### Enable or disable the built-in browser\n\nClaude can use the web in Cowork in two ways: a browser built into the Claude Desktop app, or your users' own Chrome browser through the Claude in Chrome extension. You can enable one, both, or neither.\n\n  * Built-in browser: Controlled from Organization settings > Cowork. On Team plans, it's on by default as it rolls out this week. Team owners can turn it off anytime. On Enterprise plans, it's off by default at launch and turns on by default starting September 10, 2026, unless you've turned it off. When it's off, users can't open the built-in browser and Claude can't use it.\n\n  * Claude in Chrome: Controlled from Organization settings > Claude in Chrome, and users' browsers still need the extension deployed or installed. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBlog | Claude by Anthropic (https://claude.com/blog?cc61befa_page=2&d7430fcd_page=3&query=CTA)\nciteturn843search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; ## Claude Cowork and chat are now one ClaudeSeptember 16, 2026\n\n# Blog\n\nProduct news and best practices for teams building with Claude.\n\n## Claude Cowork and chat are now one Claude\n\nSeptember 16, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude for Small Business launches new workflows, integrations, and training programs\n\nSeptember 15, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude in Chrome is generally available\n\nAugust 26, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude gets its own browser in Cowork\n\nAugust 26, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude Code now supports artifacts\n\nJune 18, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Building intelligent apps for Apple platforms with Claude in the Foundation Models framework\n\nJune 8, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## New in Claude Managed Agents: self-hosted sandboxes and MCP tunnels\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## New in Claude Managed Agents: dreaming, outcomes, and multiagent orchestration\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## New connectors in Claude for everyday life\n\nApril 23, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Built-in memory for Claude Managed Agents\n\nApril 23, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude Cowork and chat are now one Claude\n\nSeptember 16, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude for Small Business launches new workflows, integrations, and training programs\n\nSeptember 15, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude in Chrome is generally available\n\nAugust 26, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude gets its own browser in Cowork\n\nAugust 26, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Claude Code now supports artifacts\n\nJune 18, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## Building intelligent apps for Apple platforms with Claude in the Foundation Models framework\n\nJune 8, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## New in Claude Managed Agents: self-hosted sandboxes and MCP tunnels\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n## New in Claude Managed Agents: dreaming, outcomes, and multiagent orchestration\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\nRead moreRead more\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAI at Meta: Meta AI Products, Models and Research (https://ai.meta.com/events/)\nciteturn843search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Introducing Muse: The World’s First Personal AI Agent Built for Everyone SEP 8, 2026 ... About\n\n# Introducing Muse: Your personal AI agent\n\nTry Muse\n\nLearn more\n\n# Introducing Muse: Your personal AI agent\n\nTry Muse\n\nLearn more\n\n## WHAT'S NEW\n\nIntroducing Muse: The World’s First Personal AI Agent Built for Everyone SEP 8, 2026\n\nHow We Built Safety Into Muse SEP 8, 2026\n\nHow We Designed Muse SEP 8, 2026\n\nIntroducing Muse Spark 1.3 SEP 2, 2026\n\n## META AI\n\n### More ways to use Meta AI\n\nExplore features\n\nImage: Meta AI app graphic\n\n#### Meta AI app\n\nAn improved Meta AI assistant means you can ask anything, anytime and get more helpful answers wherever you are.\n\nAsk Meta AI\n\nLearn more\n\nImage: Muse Spark grid\n\n#### Image creation with our new model, Muse Image\n\nExplore fun presets, make precise edits and visualize your ideas.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow We Built Safety Into Muse | Meta AI Research (https://research.meta.ai/blog/security-and-safety-for-ai-agents-our-approach-with-muse)\nciteturn843search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: today; September 8, 2026·20 minute read ... Today we launched Muse — our personal agent. ... Muse uses a special browser sub-agent to complete each task — reading the pages, traversing the site, filling forms, etc.This sub-agent has similar, web specific instructions about which parts of the content may be adversarial. ... Similarly, if Muse makes a restaurant reservation for you or helps you find a great product on Facebook Marketplace, that may also indirectly influence the ads you see.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n세계 최초의 모두를 위한 개인 AI 에이전트, Muse를 소개합니다 | Meta 소개 (https://about.fb.com/ko/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-the-worlds-first-personal-ai-agent-built-for-everyone/amp/)\nciteturn843search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: today; Muse는 평소 소통하는 방식을 기반으로 설계돼, Muse 앱이나 WhatsApp에서 다른 사람에게 메시지를 보내듯 Muse와 자연스럽게 대화할 수 있습니다.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n#muse #metaai #productinnovation | Nicola Mendelsohn CBE (https://www.linkedin.com/posts/nicolamendelsohn1_muse-metaai-productinnovation-activity-7503173937061752833-1KbQ)\nciteturn843search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Learn more about Muse here: https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWeatherNext 3: Our most advanced global weather AI model (https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/introducing-weathernext-3/)\nciteturn843search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: today; Sep 03, 2026 ... Today, Google DeepMind and Google Research are introducing WeatherNext 3, the most advanced and accurate global weather model to date, according to independent live evaluations by Brightband.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMUSE: An Interactive Meta-Agent for Understanding and Steering LLM-powered Data Science Systems (https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.16181)\nciteturn843academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Title: MUSE: An Interactive Meta-Agent for Understanding and Steering LLM-powered Data Science Systems ... Date: Mon Aug 17 06:54:01 2026\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMeta launches personal AI agent, Muse, emphasizes safety and privacy (https://apnews.com/article/3a4572eb4cf4e95d8a0dfdad6e6ca065)\nciteturn843news14 [wordlim: 100] Published: last week; Date: Tue Sep  8 19:05:55 2026 UTCMeta launched on Tuesday a personal artificial intelligence agent, Muse, for people 18 and over who are looking for help with day-to-day tasks like schedules, shopping and, in the company's words, turning \"long-term goals into action plans.\"The parent company of Instagram and Facebook is stressing the safety and privacy features of the agent, which for now is only available in the U.S.\nMeta launches personal AI agent, Muse, emphasizes safety and privacy\nDate: Tue Sep  8 19:05:55 2026 UTC\n\nMeta launched on Tuesday a personal artificial intelligence agent, Muse, for people 18 and over who are looking for help with day-to-day tasks like schedules, shopping and, in the company's words, turning \"long-term goals into action plans.\" \nThe parent company of Instagram and Facebook is stressing the safety and privacy features of the agent, which for now is only available in the U.S. Muse, Meta said, runs on a dedicated, secure virtual machine that houses both the agent and the user's data. \nPeople can message the agent in a separate app, called Muse, or message it in WhatsApp. It can handle simple tasks like sending an email or booking travel, or bigger, long-term goals like creating a yearlong exercise plan or setting up a new business. \n\"Once a person shares a goal with Muse, it helps them develop a personalized plan and coordinate their time and resources, then advances the work on its own. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMeta debuts Muse Spark 1.3 as personal agent work continues (https://www.axios.com/2026/09/02/meta-debuts-muse-spark-13-as-personal-agent-work-continues)\nciteturn843news15 [wordlim: 100] Published: 2 weeks ago; Meta debuts Muse Spark 1.3 as personal agent work continuesDate: Wed Sep  2 19:10:34 2026 UTC\nMeta debuts Muse Spark 1.3 as personal agent work continues\nDate: Wed Sep  2 19:10:34 2026 UTC\n\nMeta debuts Muse Spark 1.3 as personal agent work continues\n\nMeta on Wednesday released Muse Spark 1.3, an update it says significantly improves performance in coding and agentic tasks.\nWhy it matters: Meta is trying to keep pace with Anthropic, OpenAI and Google, which all made major model announcements this week.\nState of play: Meta AI chief Alexandr Wang told Axios the update helps pave the way for upcoming products, such as personal agents.\nThe big picture: Meta's release comes amid a flurry of model updates from across the industry.\nZoom in: Muse Spark 1.3 is priced the same as its predecessor, which Wang characterized as \"aggressive.\"\nBetween the lines: With more powerful models, there is also more attention on safety, Wang said.\nYes, but: Unlike other leading labs, Wang says Meta didn't find it necessary to pause any work to address safety concerns.\nMuse Spark 1.3 will roll out Wednesday in Muse Code and Meta's API. \nWhat we're watching: Whether Meta will continue to close the gap with Anthropic, OpenAI and Google and how its model improvements - especially in agentic work - show up in Meta's products.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBlack Holes and Revel-AI-tions - Meta's new personal AI agent accused of stealing social media handles from top British band Muse (https://www.techradar.com/pro/black-holes-and-revel-ai-tions-metas-new-personal-ai-agent-accused-of-stealing-social-media-handles-from-top-british-band-muse)\nciteturn843news16 [wordlim: 100] Published: last week; After Meta recently launched Muse, its new \"personal AI agent\", the company has apparently already run into difficulties securing the social media handles for its new project. ... best bug in twitter history pic.twitter.com/0VORftYfPn September 8, 2026 ... Of course, there might only be a limited number of words and names available for new projects and products, especially with terms as historic and iconic as Muse (which dates back to Ancient Greece), but Meta's move does raise concerns about the ability of powerful organizations to dominate and commandeer entities such as usernames.\nBlack Holes and Revel-AI-tions - Meta's new personal AI agent accused of stealing social media handles from top British band Muse\nDate: Thu Sep 10 16:05:00 2026 UTC\n\nAfter Meta recently launched Muse, its new \"personal AI agent\", the company has apparently already run into difficulties securing the social media handles for its new project.\nBoth the Instagram and Threads handle for @Muse previously belonged to iconic British rock trio Muse, but now appear to be under the control of Meta.\nThe former has apparently been shunted out to @Museband, despite having been around a lot longer than Meta's latest misguided AI boondoggle - with the move alarming fans and industry observers around the world.\n\nJust a load of Hysteria?\n\nOne of Britain's most successful rock exports, Muse (the band) trademarked its name in 1999, and had used the @muse account on Instagram and on X for many years.\nHowever The Independent noticed that in July 2026, this changed, with Meta's platform taking over on both websites. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMeta just launched an AI that can actually run your life online - here's what Muse can do (https://www.tomsguide.com/ai/meta-just-launched-an-ai-that-can-actually-run-your-life-online-heres-what-muse-can-do)\nciteturn843news17 [wordlim: 100] Published: last week; Date: Wed Sep  9 12:14:12 2026 UTCMeta has launched Muse, a new personal AI agent designed to work across the apps and services you already use.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMark Zuckerberg's Muse personal AI agent is a work accessory designed by people who don't do real work (https://www.techradar.com/pro/mark-zuckerbergs-muse-personal-ai-agent-is-a-work-accessory-designed-by-people-who-dont-do-real-work)\nciteturn843news18 [wordlim: 100] Published: last week; Mark Zuckerberg's Muse personal AI agent is a work accessory designed by people who don't do real workDate: Sat Sep 12 11:00:00 2026 UTC\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMUSE: Agentic 3D Scene Authoring via Memory-Grounded Incremental Requirement Satisfaction (https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.14168)\nciteturn843academia19 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; In this paper, we present MUSE, a memory-grounded multi-agent framework in which an Architect compiles instructions into structured requirements, a Sculptor executes local scene operations, and an Inspector verifies each step while updating Working, Scene, and Skill Memory. ... On full construction cases, MUSE improves All-Goal success from 37.9 to 80.7 and surface-constraint fulfillment from 35.0 to 92.6 over the strongest baseline.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMUSE: A Multi-agent Framework for Unconstrained Story Envisioning via Closed-Loop Cognitive Orchestration (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.03028)\nciteturn843academia20 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Title: MUSE: A Multi-agent Framework for Unconstrained Story Envisioning via Closed-Loop Cognitive Orchestration ... Date: Tue Feb  3 02:55:00 2026\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn843view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-18.json\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn843view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-18/transcript.md\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n"
